<title>COMOROS: Comoros welcomes U.S. firm's $256 million port project.</title>
<headline>Comoros welcomes U.S. firm's $256 million port project.</headline>
<dateline>MORONI 1997-03-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Comoros government, beset by social and economic crises, has welcomed an undertaking by an American firm to build a free port, shipyard, floating dock and a fish processing unit in the Indian Ocean island republic.</p>
<p>The project, valued at $256 million -- more than nine times the country's annual budget -- is intended to form the basis of a large-scale fishing operation based on the Comoros.</p>
<p>Lucien Forbes, head of the sponsoring company based in Rhode Island, told Reuters on Sunday: &quot;This is not a grandiose project when put in a regional context.</p>
</text>
